WEBVTT

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:10.860
<i>A search of the room belonging 
to the vampire girl serving Physis</i>

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:15.740
<i>revealed that she was investigating 
a certain rumor on campus.</i>

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.800
<i>One about a ghost in the 
ruins of the old library.</i>

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:26.380
Most of the records on the school
 were lost in a fire.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.530
When the old library burned down?

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.760
It's said that the head librarian at the time

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.260
was a double agent for Physis.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.260
That can't be!

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.280
His name was Genius.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.140
And it was Faria's ancestor, 
Eunomia, who defeated him.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:49.150
They say Genius's curse 
continues to haunt this school.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:50.780
You mean he...

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:53.780
It's a popular ghost story.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.030
Gareth!

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.040
Claire?

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.210
I brought you those records 
you wanted about the old library.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:05.540
Thank you.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:10.450
Er, do you mind if I ask why 
you're looking into the old library?

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.670
The site is off-limits, you know!

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.300
And there's a rumor about a ghost...

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.300
I appreciate the help.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.500
U-Um!

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.930
If there's anything else 
you need me to investigate, I'll—

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.100
No, this is sufficient for now.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.550
If you'll excuse me.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.230
I just want to help...

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:09.640
<b>Holiday\h\h\h-Festival-</b>

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:06.390
It sure is lively, isn't it?

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.450
The school festival is coming up.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.460
School festival?

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.710
It's a celebration put on
 by the student body.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.520
There will be a variety 
of exhibitions and events.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.460
It's a most exciting time.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.630
The student council even...

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:21.470
Huh?

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.720
What is it?

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.100
The door's a bit stuck.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.850
May I?

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.020
Separation is one of the 
fundamentals of alchemy.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.860
Thank you again, Claire.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:45.130
Personally, I wish I was better 
at attachment than separation...

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.300
Oh, Gareth...

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.200
You really are in love 
with Gareth, aren't you?

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.880
W-W-Well, you don't have to just 
come out and say it like that...

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:00.130
Though I guess it is pretty obvious...

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.480
Love?

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:02.380
Nemo?

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:07.130
Oh, I was just thinking about 
what that really means.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:09.520
How philosophical!

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:15.900
For me, when I think of Gareth, 
my heart aches and flutters.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.400
When you think of him?

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:22.530
Yes! He saved me from a monster once,

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:27.400
and I've admired him
 like a prince ever since!

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:33.340
Admiration? Is that what love means?

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:40.920
I was hoping to invite him to the dance...

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.330
What dance?

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:46.470
It's a nighttime tradition
 at the school festival.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:50.310
It's brought lots of couples together!

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:56.690
But... I'm sure Gareth wouldn't want me.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:59.440
I'm no help to him at all.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.980
You're really okay leaving things like this?

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:09.070
You may regret it later,
and you may never get another chance.

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:13.020
Besides, we could die at any time.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:17.100
That's a bit extreme.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.150
Is it?

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.130
But he does have a point.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.540
I think it's good to be brave.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.780
President...

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:26.320
Nemo...

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:29.210
Yes, you're right.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.800
I don't want to regret this.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:35.220
I'll ask Gareth to the dance, 
even if I'm doomed to fail!

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.420
Good. That's the spirit.

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:38.890
Thank you!

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:41.190
Speaking of...

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:44.270
Have you decided who you'll 
be dancing with, President?

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:45.320
Me?

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.570
Actually...

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.450
No, never mind.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.950
Oho! I see, I see.

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:58.330
Let's both be brave, President!

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:01.210
What? Wait, that isn't what I—

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:08.340
Who I wanna dance with the 
night of the festival, huh?

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:10.670
What a great question, Nemo!

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:11.520
That's—

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:14.460
His beloved Miss Sophitia, right?

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:15.980
You a mind-reader or somethin'?!

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:17.750
When'd you learn to do that?!

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:20.850
It'd be more shocking if I <i>hadn't</i> guessed it.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:24.240
So you love Sophitia, Jou?

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:29.070
H-Hey! Don't just come out 
and say it like that...

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.990
I'm seeing a lot of that body language today.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:35.570
Looks like the big man is still 
just a kid when it comes to love.

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:38.060
Shaddap! What about you?

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:38.620
Me?

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:40.620
I'm free right now.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:43.090
The heck? Then we're in the same boat—

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:47.310
Given my position, 
it's difficult to pick a favorite.

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:49.240
Go figure, Mr. Prince...

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.850
Say, Nemo, how are things going 
with you and the president of late?

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.350
With me and Faria? Why do you ask?

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:57.800
Wow, he's got the oblivious act down pat.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.800
She spent your recovery 
nursing you back to health.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:02.440
I thought you were well on your way.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:05.360
There you are.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:07.360
Shirley?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.410
Nemo,

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:12.100
do you know who you'll be dancing 
with at the school festival yet?

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.990
No, no idea.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:14.870
I see.

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:19.000
Then might I reserve that honor?

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:21.950
Think about it.

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:22.880
Till next time.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:25.680
Whoa, whoa...

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:28.630
I've never seen the iron lady of the 
disciplinary committee like that...

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.130
Nemo, did something go down 
between you and Shirley?

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:36.350
That's a secret, I think?

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.500
Seriously? What happened?!

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:40.730
Yeah, you gotta fill us in!

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.420
Spill the beans!

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.720
I told you, it's a secret...

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:44.520
You're not gonna tell us?!

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:44.520
Talk!

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.740
And now, it's time to decide 
the student council's event.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.690
Yeah!

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:52.110
The moment has come!

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:53.660
Our event?

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:59.500
What the Seven Knights will 
be doing for the school festival.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.120
Does anyone have any ideas?

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:01.840
Me, me!

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.300
Cafés are totally cliché.

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.220
What about a chic bar or something?

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:07.060
Overruled by the disciplinary committee.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.630
I'm drinking age in my country, though...

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:14.670
Okay, how about a thrilling fighting 
tournament?! Them against us!

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:17.150
No, that sounds exhausting.

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:21.800
It's not exhausting! What's wrong with you?

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:21.140
This is foolish.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:23.640
Gareth?

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:26.790
Doesn't this all seem a bit frivolous to you?

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.900
We've barely found any clues 
regarding Physis's presence here.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.280
Physis...

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:32.400
But...

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.790
We should set an example 
for the other students

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:38.780
and show them it's acceptable
 to relieve stress.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.730
What a surprising show of support!

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:43.500
Say, Shirley, I think you've 
loosened up a bit lately.

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:45.500
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.660
I see.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:48.360
Do as you like, then.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.130
And I'll do the same.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:53.240
Don't worry. I'll help out
with whatever you decide.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.340
Well, can't blame the guy.

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:00.980
His hometown was razed by 
the servants of destruction,

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:03.140
so he hates them more than most of us.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.770
Physis destroyed his home?

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:11.020
Well, let's get back to brainstorming!

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.340
I want an all-day bar—

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:13.120
Overruled.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:13.600
Then a maid—

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:14.160
Overruled.

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:15.520
Then a fighting tournament—

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:16.270
Overruled!

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:21.890
Excuse me!

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.970
I'm sorry, but could you please 
not bother me right now?

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:27.020
It's not like that!

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:30.280
I want to help more with your investigation.

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:35.100
I was thinking that searching the old 
Alchemy Research Institute records

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:36.680
might yield something.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:38.110
But that's...

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:40.050
I want to help you!

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:41.560
Please let me!

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:49.190
I have no way to repay you.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:51.070
That isn't true.

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:57.840
Just be my partner for the student festival.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:59.640
That's all I want.

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:04.650
Very well.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.170
Really?

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:09.850
I'll do my best, then.

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:11.210
And if I find anything, let's dance!

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:12.710
It's a promise!

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:21.660
I'm a cruel man.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.730
Wow!

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.490
Oh, woe is me!

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:42.870
My beloved was a servant of destruction!

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.820
What a tragedy!

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:48.580
Thus the old library was 
consumed in flame,

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:53.190
and everything related to it was cursed!

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.510
Stuck with a café in the end...

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:06.180
A tournament or martial arts
 demonstration woulda been better.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:07.180
Yeah, yeah.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:08.890
Quit whining and get to work.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:11.630
Here you are, my ladies.

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:15.470
Gildan's really taken to this.

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:21.410
Well, the rest of the student body 
really admires the Seven Knights.

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:23.140
Honestly.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.820
I do believe we have 
better things to be doing.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:30.160
You there. Tell me your order at once.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.370
R-Right!

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.740
Gareth is so cold,

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:35.620
but we love that about him!

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:38.590
Well, I guess that's fine...

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:40.020
Pardon.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:41.880
Could I get some help in the kitchen?

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:43.560
I'd be happy to—

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:44.780
No, no, no, no!

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:46.580
You stay with the customers, President!

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:47.930
I got this!

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:51.390
You'd take us from a café 
to a croquette stall.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.800
This has turned out to be so much fun.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:55.900
Nemo?

00:11:56.430 --> 00:12:00.780
It's so nice to do something 
other than battle with you guys.

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:04.410
How true.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.680
Um, by the way, Nemo...

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:13.970
About the dance tonight...

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.890
If you wouldn't mind...

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:21.050
I was wondering if you'd be my partner.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:24.800
Oh, actually, Shirley already asked me.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:25.550
What?

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:28.560
I-Indeed.

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:29.820
I did.

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:32.810
Coming right up!

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:35.900
This is perfect timing, Nemo.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.460
Will you give me your answer now?

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:41.390
Who would you rather dance with?
 Me or Shirley?

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:43.770
Er... Do I have to choose?

00:12:43.770 --> 00:12:44.820
You do!

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:48.150
I c-can't dance with both of you?

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:49.760
Of course not!

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:51.700
You only get one dance partner.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:53.580
You have to make up your mind!

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.830
W-Well...

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:56.910
Hey, Nemo!

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:59.210
Could you take this to Miss Sophitia?

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:01.040
Oh, sure!

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:01.770
Sorry.

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:02.930
Let's talk later!

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:05.220
Hey!

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:10.990
<i>The dance, eh?</i>

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:13.820
Thank you.

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:15.480
I so love croquettes!

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:18.980
You seem to be enjoying the school festival.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:20.850
Yes, I suppose...

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.930
Um, could I ask you something?

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:27.490
Of course. I'm happy to be of service.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:29.730
I don't really get it.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.990
If you admire someone 
and want to be with them...

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:36.000
That's love, isn't it?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:40.000
That's right, although 
love takes many forms.

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:42.460
When people fall in love,

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:45.260
they begin to behave differently.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:49.860
But unlike them, 
that hasn't happened to me.

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:53.270
So what is it I'm feeling?

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.480
This emotion...

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:00.730
I was wondering if it's 
something other than love.

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.090
I see.

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:06.490
You're going through adolescence.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.870
Adolescence?

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:11.200
It's a normal part of growing up.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:16.000
I believe what you're feeling may 
fall under the category of love.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.250
You think so?

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:22.920
Love is the desire to help the one you love.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:27.630
But everyone expresses 
that in a different way.

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:32.320
And a single person can be 
in love with many people,

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:35.650
just with different orders of priority.

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:37.640
Priority?

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:41.400
You mean... like choosing 
someone over someone else?

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.420
Yes.

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:45.010
Though it would be preferable 
if we didn't have to choose

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:50.870
and could simply love everyone equally.

00:14:57.180 --> 00:14:59.080
You're late, Nemo.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:00.500
The café's closed.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.900
Oh, sorry.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:03.650
Where's Faria?

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:06.860
She went to the student 
council room with Ellen.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:09.270
She's a workaholic, even on days like this.

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:10.510
Really?

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.580
I heard the whole thing, loverboy.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:15.680
You got yourself an invitation 
from both Shirley <i>and</i> the president.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:18.190
Which one are you gonna dance with?

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:20.250
It's almost time for the dance,

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:21.770
so there's not much time to lose!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:24.120
Well, actually...

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:34.420
Do you have an answer for me?

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:36.280
About that, Shirley...

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:39.060
I was wondering if, rather than me,

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:41.910
you wanted to ask Ellen.

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:46.170
She's the one you were 
really watching earlier,

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:49.660
so I thought that might be
 how you really felt.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:53.680
I can't ask her.

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:55.470
Shirley?

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:57.350
I'm a vampire.

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:59.940
I can't live without Ellen.

00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:05.360
But it's an unrequited need...

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:07.970
I don't know how Ellen feels.

00:16:07.970 --> 00:16:11.360
She'd never approach me on her own.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.500
I don't know exactly how I feel either.

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.830
It's possible I invited you out of spite,

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:19.380
to vent my frustration.

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:23.260
I'm rather devious, aren't I?

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:25.610
I'm sorry.

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:29.060
I won't be dancing with anyone after all.

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:30.280
Shirley...

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:37.010
Shirley! I don't know 
where the furniture goes.

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:39.040
Coming!

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:52.830
It's almost time for the dance.

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.620
What'll I do?

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:57.030
I really need to find something.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:17:01.730
But of course there's nothing left 
here at the old library.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:09.080
Ow, ow, ow...

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:11.340
Where am I?

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:18.700
Is this a door?

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:22.680
It won't open.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:27.010
Maybe I can apply a form of separation...

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:34.180
It worked!

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:38.960
If I find something and make it back...

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:42.530
I'll be helping Gareth, won't I?

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.550
The dance is about to start.

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:57.610
I told you I wasn't going 
to dance with anyone.

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:02.140
Someone told me once...

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:06.810
that everyone expresses
 their love differently.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:13.260
I think people change when they fall in love.

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:17.070
So don't you think it's all right?

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:19.660
If you're a little devious about it.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:20.710
Nemo...

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:27.730
When I really think about it, 
she's the most devious of all.

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:28.710
You mean Ellen?

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:30.140
Yes.

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:34.220
Always smiling and claiming
 to just go with the flow...

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:40.890
The dance might be the perfect 
way to bring things to light.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:42.730
Shirley...

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:44.280
Thank you, Nemo.

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:46.720
You've helped me to make up my mind.

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:49.010
Now...

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:51.230
You'll be dancing
 with the president, won't you?

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:56.380
She's one person without a 
trace of deviousness in her.

00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:58.510
You had better not make her cry.

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:01.260
Right.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.250
Ellen, may I have a moment?

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.280
Sure.

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:15.400
As for you, President...

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:29.030
I-Is this the right way?

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:31.390
Yes. You're doing quite well, Nemo.

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:35.900
There's still a lot I don't understand,

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:38.400
but there is one thing I know for sure...

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:43.160
I'm so glad I met you all!

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:44.630
Nemo...

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:09.200
This book...

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:12.200
Is that a seal of some kind?

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:25.580
She's not coming, then?

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:29.480
Gareth.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:32.830
Claire... Where have you been?

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.940
I'm not entirely sure.

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:37.680
Um, I'm really sorry.

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:39.830
I couldn't find anything.

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:41.830
That's all right.

00:20:42.810 --> 00:20:44.690
We should hurry before it's over.

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:48.780
Did we not promise to dance?

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:53.130
Yes!

00:20:58.810 --> 00:20:59.940
I'm so happy.

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:04.610
Dancing with you is like a dream.

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:06.350
Surely not.

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:09.100
It's true. Right now...

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:14.220
I'm the happiest I've ever been.

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:17.360
Really?

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:23.910
Oh, wait.

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:26.550
I just remembered...

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:30.090
I have to tell you...

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:34.780
In the old... library...

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:46.450
Claire—

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:52.980
Claire!

00:23:25.520 --> 00:23:28.560
No one can escape sorrow.

00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:30.650
How do I atone for my sin?

00:23:30.650 --> 00:23:33.080
We just have to keep moving forward.

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:34.590
Destroy Physis!

00:23:34.590 --> 00:23:36.470
Next time: "Apocalypse."

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Sortie -Apocalypse-</b>

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.450
I'll take up the sword once more
 to atone for what I've done.
